  "passed_evidence": [
    "The exact dataset, frozen sources, hourly lattice, 2192 complete UTC days and two byte-identical runs passed every integrity gate.",
    "The primary produced positive Normal and Stress returns in Design and Validation, ended flat, and stayed within the frozen turnover, holding, stress-drawdown and episode-concentration limits.",
    "Design exceeded buy-and-hold by 87.88761019 percentage points, reduced maximum drawdown by 22.20173931 percentage points and achieved 2.35566869 times passive Calmar.",
    "The primary reduced drawdown versus buy-and-hold in all five annual windows and produced positive Normal and Stress returns in four of five years."
  ],
  "material_learning": "Daily MACD 12/26/9 positive histogram was a strong Design-period momentum state and consistently reduced annual drawdown, but it did not generalize to 2023-2024 risk-adjusted quality. Validation captured only 37.983663 percent of passive upside and reached 67.473255 percent of passive Calmar despite reducing maximum drawdown by 14.10998772 percentage points. Fast-length neighbors 10 and 14 captured only 37.015634 and 39.102217 percent of upside and reached 63.040249 and 68.436819 percent of passive Calmar. Only two of five years reached 75 percent of passive Calmar, only three reached 50 percent upside capture, and 63.02320442 percent of positive annual return was concentrated in 2020. The family therefore represents regime-dependent exposure reduction, not stable independent risk-adjusted alpha.",
  "scientific_claim": "The exact daily complete-UTC-day MACD histogram policy using TradingView-style EMA initialization and preregistered fast lengths 10, 12 and 14 with slow 26 and signal 9 produced positive after-cost historical returns but failed frozen Validation upside-capture, Calmar, neighbor-stability, annual-breadth and year-concentration gates. None is a candidate, and the result does not authorize selecting fast length 14, changing any EMA length or initialization, adding a threshold, confirmation, stop, DRA interaction or ensemble.",
